WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.400
Even before the first Covid-19 vaccine was&nbsp;
around in Germany in December 2020 – protests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.680
against the jab had already started!  
 
At Germany’s largest demonstration, over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.200
30,000 people gathered to speak up against looming&nbsp;
vaccinations and anti-covid restrictions. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:29.840
They kept going throughout the&nbsp;
pandemic – loud and big! 
 
 &nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.480
The majority of Germans couldn’t wait to get&nbsp;
vaccinated – But there is a significant minority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.160
of sceptics who have so far refused the jab.  
 
The many burdens of the Covid-19 pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.760
have caused divisions, split up&nbsp;
friendships and even families.  
 
 

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.680
In this video I want to find out:&nbsp;
How did we get here? Why are some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.240
people sceptical of vaccinations? And how&nbsp;
should we react to this scepticism?  
 &nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.840
In order to answer these questions,&nbsp;
let’s look into some history books. 
 
 &nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.640
Anti-Vaxx movements are as old&nbsp;
as vaccinations themselves. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.160
In 1796 the English physician Edward Jenner&nbsp;
developed what today is called the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.280
vaccination. It was against smallpox - an&nbsp;
illness that killed tens of thousands each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:37.040
year in Europe alone at the time.  
 
Also, common back then: cowpox. Jenner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.600
observed that people who had previously&nbsp;
had cowpox were immune to smallpox. 
&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.240
The physician took fluid from a blister of&nbsp;
a woman infected with cowpox and scratched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.640
it into the skin of a young boy.  
 
Six weeks on, Jenner infected the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.600
boy with smallpox – but the kid didn’t&nbsp;
get sick. The immunization had worked. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:02.160
An important side note: the word vaccination&nbsp;
comes from the Latin word “Vacca”, meaning cow. 
 &nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.680
The medical revolution saved countless&nbsp;
lives. But at the time, it triggered fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.240
and scepticism in the United Kingdom - and&nbsp;
when it came to Germany, there as well. 
 

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:36.240
History shows us: Scepticism against&nbsp;
vaccinations has always been there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.880
When we look at the situation&nbsp;
today, we can still see it:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.680
about one in four people in Germany is&nbsp;
still unvaccinated – although the jabs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.960
have been around for more than a year.  
 
 
I asked myself – why do so many people still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.800
decide not to get vaccinated today?&nbsp;
Are they scared of something? 
 

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:00.880
Sabine Schroeder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.600
doesn’t deny the existence of Covid-19.&nbsp;
She is a nurse in a Covid ward herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:35.280
But she is also an alternative healer and&nbsp;
believes that vaccinations are unnatural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.280
and is scared of alleged side-effects. 
 

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:00.960
A relatively big group of vaxx sceptics in&nbsp;
Germany shares Sabine Schröder’s opinion.&nbsp;

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.280
A movement of people that also believes&nbsp;
in alternative medicine or esoterics. 
 

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.120
Supporters assume that diseases don’t happen&nbsp;
randomly. On the contrary: They believe they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.880
mark disbalances between body, mind and spirit.
Some people therefore decide not to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:37.120
vaccinated in order to keep this balance. 
 
The group is particularly strong in Germany,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.240
Austria and the German-speaking part of&nbsp;
Switzerland. When Germany’s vaccination drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:47.360
slowed down in summer 2021, even foreign&nbsp;
media-outlets reported on the movement.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.160
Not everyone in Germany who decides against the&nbsp;
jab believes solely in alternative medicine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:02.080
There is a variety of reasons. For example this&nbsp;
physiotherapist, who wants to stay anonymous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:09.840
She opposes the idea of compulsory vaccinations.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.920
Some people simply question the effectiveness&nbsp;
of Covid 19 vaccines despite scientifically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.000
proven evidence. Like this young man&nbsp;
who also wants to stay anonymous.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.200
Speaking to unvaccinated people helped me&nbsp;
get a sense for their individual reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.240
And I also realized:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.360
There is a lot of misinformation around.  
 
So to get the full picture, I spoke to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.920
scientists from the University of Erfurt.
And their results confirmed my impression:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:29.200
There is not just ONE reason to&nbsp;
refuse the jab.The group is diverse.&nbsp;

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.840
Nevertheless, the researchers were&nbsp;
able to identify 5 main reasons.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.480
Number one: Confidence 
&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:43.280
People in this group question the safety and&nbsp;
the effectiveness of Covid-19 vaccinations.  
 &nbsp;

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.760
They also distrust the&nbsp;
health care system in general

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.800
The 2nd reason: Complacency  
 
This group tends to overestimate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.840
their own immune system and underestimate&nbsp;
the risk of a severe Covid-19 infection.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.920
Three: Constraints 
 
People in this group believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:04.880
in the effectiveness of the jab but feel that&nbsp;
it takes too much time and effort to get it.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:08.560
Four: Calculation 
 
They consciously evaluate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:15.120
the benefits and the risks of a vaccination.
They are particularly prone to fake news spread o

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:21.200
And the last one: Collective Responsibility 
 
 
These people don’t question the jab, but they rely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:26.160
on others to get it. They don’t feel the social&nbsp;
responsibility to get vaccinated themselves.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.120
These 5 reasons don’t stand alone –&nbsp;
they can overlap and come together. 
 
 
 &nbsp;

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.920
Looking at scepticism from&nbsp;
different angles, one realizes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:57.840
reasons to refuse the jab are complex, and they&nbsp;
have always been part of the story of vaccination.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.880
The question is now: Do we just&nbsp;
have to accept this scepticism?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:11.840
Do we need compulsory vaccinations?&nbsp;
Or are there other solutions?

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.120
Germany discusses plans for&nbsp;
mandatory Covid vaccinations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:25.840
Opinions on the topic vary. The country’s&nbsp;
health minister supports the idea. 
 
 
 &nbsp;

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.560
Others emphasize the potential danger behind&nbsp;
the measure: a crack in social cohesion. 
 
 &nbsp;

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.560
Aversion and annoyance have already grown&nbsp;
in the last two years of the pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:07.840
experts observed. 
 
&nbsp;

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:16.880
The ever-changing Covid 19 restrictions,&nbsp;
varying regulations across German states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:21.360
and inconsistent information provided by&nbsp;
authorities are said to be influencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.760
this trend. 
 
 
 
Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:28.080
social cohesion has been affected by lockdown&nbsp;
measures and limited personal contact. 
 
 
 
 &nbsp;

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:48.080
Should the threat of Covid-19 decline soon,&nbsp;
then the anger on boths sides might also fade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:53.360
away. And once people get their social lives&nbsp;
back, social cohesion can surely improve.  
 &nbsp;

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.480
And when the long-term effects of the&nbsp;
pandemic become visible in society,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:03.840
we might well need new ways to repair this unity.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:10.160
you

